-- The Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law, 5786-2026, s 4: a limit on application.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are generated from line N of the deposited transcription.
--
-- WHAT THIS SECTION DOES.  It switches the whole Law off, "מיום תחילתן", for an individual who ceased
-- to be an Israeli resident during tax year 2028 or 2029 and stayed in Israel fewer than 75 days in
-- one of those years.  The words "מיום תחילתן" put the start at the commencement of the provisions, 1
-- January 2026 (s 6), so the disapplication reaches the exemption of every tax year, 2026 onward: a
-- clawback that depends on facts of 2028 or 2029 (NOTES.md fork register, F10: the text decides, noted).
--
-- WHAT IS AN INPUT.  The day the person ceased to be an Israeli resident, and the days spent in Israel
-- in 2028 and in 2029, are facts of the individual (il36-nouns.l4).
--
-- FORK F9, "באחת מאותן השנים": the 75-day test is applied in one of "those years", 2028 or 2029.
-- Reading A: in either year, whichever year the person ceased to be a resident.  Reading B: in the
-- year the person ceased to be a resident.  B implies A.  They differ for a person who ceased in one
-- of the years and stayed 75 days or more in that year but fewer than 75 in the other.

§ `Section 4 — a limit on application`

-- src:33 | הוראות חוק זה לא יחולו מיום תחילתן על יחיד אשר חדל להיות תושב ישראל במהלך אחת משנות המס 2028 או 2029 ושהה בישראל פחות מ־75 ימים באחת מאותן השנים.
@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 4 (transcription line 33): "חדל להיות תושב ישראל במהלך אחת משנות המס 2028 או 2029"
GIVEN `the person` IS AN `An individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 — the person ceased to be an Israeli resident during tax year 2028 or 2029` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`'s `the day the person ceased to be an Israeli resident`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST day THEN    DATE_YEAR day EQUALS 2028
                       OR DATE_YEAR day EQUALS 2029

@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 4 (transcription line 33): "ושהה בישראל פחות מ־75 ימים באחת מאותן השנים"; fork F9
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 — the person stayed in Israel fewer than 75 days in one of those years, at the readings` `the readings` `:` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the readings`'s `the reading of the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`
    WHEN `section 4 counts the days in Israel in either 2028 or 2029, whichever year the person ceased to be a resident`
    THEN    `the person`'s `days spent in Israel in tax year 2028` BELOW 75
         OR `the person`'s `days spent in Israel in tax year 2029` BELOW 75
    WHEN `section 4 counts the days in Israel in the year in which the person ceased to be a resident`
    THEN CONSIDER `the person`'s `the day the person ceased to be an Israeli resident`
         WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST day THEN IF DATE_YEAR day EQUALS 2028
                            THEN `the person`'s `days spent in Israel in tax year 2028` BELOW 75
                            ELSE `the person`'s `days spent in Israel in tax year 2029` BELOW 75
    WHEN `a case that turns on the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel is declined`
    THEN `a rule that needs a concrete reading was handed a reading the text does not decide; resolve the readings first (il36-answers.l4)`

@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return Law s 4 (transcription line 33)
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 — the Law does not apply to the person, at the readings` `the readings` `:` `the person` MEANS
        `s 4 — the person ceased to be an Israeli resident during tax year 2028 or 2029` `the person`
    AND `s 4 — the person stayed in Israel fewer than 75 days in one of those years, at the readings` `the readings` `:` `the person`
